<h2>Insurance company adjuster vs. public adjuster</h2>
<p>Most people meet an insurance adjuster only after a loss, and that adjuster works for the insurance company. A public adjuster is licensed to represent the policyholder in the same claim. Here is how the two roles compare:</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Insurance company adjuster</th><th>Public adjuster</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Who they represent</td><td>The insurer</td><td>The insured policyholder</td></tr>
<tr><td>Who pays them</td><td>The insurance company (staff or independent firm)</td><td>The policyholder, under a written contract</td></tr>
